WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.520
Suppose the heritability of height in a population is 0.6.

2
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.940
Does that mean 60% of your own height comes from your genes?

3
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:19.040
It does not. Heritability describes a whole population, not one person.

4
00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.900
To see why, start with variance.

5
00:00:22.933 --> 00:00:27.753
Variance is the average squared distance of values from the mean.

6
00:00:28.573 --> 00:00:32.973
Here is a population of adults, and heights vary from person to person.

7
00:00:33.973 --> 00:00:37.273
Take each person's distance from the mean, and square it.

8
00:00:37.813 --> 00:00:40.393
The average of those squares is the variance.

9
00:00:41.453 --> 00:00:45.713
One person alone has no spread, so one person has no variance.

10
00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:52.183
Take a hypothetical height population, where the variance splits into genetic parts

11
00:00:52.183 --> 00:00:54.023
and an environmental part.

12
00:00:55.023 --> 00:00:59.803
Additive variance, the part that makes children resemble parents, is 40, from the

13
00:00:59.803 --> 00:01:01.323
average effects of alleles.

14
00:01:02.363 --> 00:01:08.323
Dominance variance is 10, interaction variance is 0, and environmental variance is

15
00:01:08.323 --> 00:01:10.643
50, so the total is 100.

16
00:01:11.523 --> 00:01:17.823
Narrow-sense heritability is additive variance over the total, 40 over 100, which is

17
00:01:17.823 --> 00:01:24.103
0.4. Broad-sense heritability adds the dominance part and gives 0.5.

18
00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:31.597
Now improve nutrition in this population, and environmental variance falls from 50

19
00:01:31.597 --> 00:01:36.857
to 20. The genetic variance stays the same, so the total is 70.

20
00:01:37.857 --> 00:01:42.077
Heritability is now 40 over 70, about 0.57.

21
00:01:42.877 --> 00:01:45.577
It went up, though no DNA changed.

22
00:01:46.297 --> 00:01:49.357
The units cancel, so heritability has none.

23
00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:53.127
High heritability does not mean fixed.

24
00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:59.207
Height is highly heritable within populations, yet average height rose across the

25
00:01:59.207 --> 00:02:05.747
twentieth century. In Richard Lewontin's analogy, a varied stock of seed is planted half

26
00:02:05.747 --> 00:02:07.927
in rich soil and half in poor.

27
00:02:08.867 --> 00:02:12.487
Within each tray, height differences are entirely genetic.

28
00:02:13.247 --> 00:02:16.407
The difference between the trays is entirely environmental.

29
00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:22.820
So heritability within a group says nothing about why groups differ.

30
00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:28.740
It cannot split one person's height into genetic and environmental parts, because

31
00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.520
one person has no variance.

32
00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:35.540
Heritability is a ratio of variances in one population.

33
00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:42.600
Keep this rule. Heritability describes a population in an environment, never a person.
